## PR Rules

- Always create PRs in **draft mode** (`gh pr create --draft`)
- Never post a comment on a PR without explicit user approval
- Never request reviewers without explicit user approval
- Never merge a PR without explicit user approval
- PR title format: `<title> ({{TICKET-PREFIX}}-XXX)`

## PR Description Format

Reviewer has 45s max. No long prose. Use this structure every time:

```markdown
## Problem
<1 sentence — what was broken or missing and why it matters>

## Fix
| | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| <behavior 1> | <old> | <new> |
| <behavior 2> | <old> | <new> |

## Key addition *(if a new abstraction/helper was introduced)*
<1-2 lines — name + purpose>

## Test
<1 line — what the tests cover>

Fixes [{{TICKET-PREFIX}}-XXX](https://{{YOUR_JIRA_ORG}}/browse/{{TICKET-PREFIX}}-XXX)
```

Rules:
- **Before/After table is mandatory** — it conveys the behavior change without reading code
- Skip "Key addition" section if no new abstraction was introduced
- No bullet-point "Changes" section listing files — reviewers read the diff
- Max 5 lines of prose total across the whole description

## PR Comment Style

- Never say "latest commit" — ambiguous if more commits land later
- Always link the specific commit SHA: `[abc1234](https://github.com/ORG/REPO/pull/NNN/commits/FULL_SHA)`
- Always reply to reviewer comments after addressing them — include the commit SHA link

---

## Git Safety

- Never auto-commit without explicit confirmation
- Never auto-push without explicit confirmation
- Always show diff and proposed commit message before committing
- Use git worktrees for parallel ticket work — never work directly on main checkout
- Always rebase on latest origin before starting work on a branch: `git fetch origin <base> && git rebase origin/<base>`
- After PR is opened for review: never rebase — merge main instead (`git fetch origin main && git merge origin/main --no-edit`). Rebase rewrites history and breaks review context.

---

## Vault Updates

- Whenever user shares a status update on a ticket, PR, or project → immediately update Dashboard.md + relevant ticket note
- Don't wait to be asked
- **DEPLOYING → DONE auto-rule**: When a Jira ticket has been in DEPLOYING state for ≥1 week, automatically transition it to DONE in Jira and update vault at the start of the next session. Track `deploying_since` date in the ticket note.

